{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel","doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError"],"title":"Sending to Mixpanel","anchor":"Sending-to-Mixpanel"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"],"title":"Encoding batches","anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"],"title":"Records left out","anchor":"Records-left-out"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","externalID":"MixpanelEncoding","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"MixpanelEncoding"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"MixpanelEncoding"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:backoff:clock:)"},{"text":" makes an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"text":") for your Mixpanel project in one call. It checks","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the project token, posts to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/track","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" endpoint of the project’s data residency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelRegion"},{"text":") with a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder"},{"text":", and splits each batch to Mixpanel’s limits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit"},{"text":"): 2,000 events and 2 MB a request. A batch with no record the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder can write, an empty one included, makes no request. It retries no response, a 5xx, 408","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and 429, waiting ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/mixpanel"},{"text":": Mixpanel’s recommended","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule, 2 s doubling to 60 s. The full jitter on top is Traffluent’s own choice. It drops and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reports any other status. The token goes in each event, so no header field is needed, and no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"trace context is sent. ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" leaves this module out; import it on its own.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The project token is public: Mixpanel’s own apps and web pages ship it. The destination takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing else. Never put the project’s secret or a service account’s credentials in an app; they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"belong to Mixpanel’s import API, for servers. The factory throws "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"empty token, and for one with a character other than a letter or digit, which no project token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The region has no default. A project’s data resides in the US, the EU or India, and Mixpanel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ingests nothing for it from another residency’s endpoint, so you pick the region on purpose.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each record becomes an event of an anonymous user. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the record’s session,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the sessions enricher, also sent as ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; a record with no session is sent under its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"own record identifier, with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Under Simplified ID Merge, Mixpanel shows a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"session’s events under ","type":"text"},{"code":"$device:<session>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and a sessionless record’s under its bare record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier. No ","type":"text"},{"code":"$user_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Its ","type":"text"},{"code":"$insert_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record’s identifier, which a redelivered record keeps, and its ","type":"text"},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the record’s timestamp in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"epoch milliseconds. The record’s vendor identifier and trace context aren’t sent. Each event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as is the endpoint’s, so Mixpanel adds no location from the request’s address. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"standard context is sent as Mixpanel’s default properties (","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_version_string","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"$app_build_number","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"$os_version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Mixpanel counts a user per ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distinct_id"},{"text":", so each session is one user in its reports, and so is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each record sent without a session. On a Mixpanel plan billed by monthly tracked users, each counts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"as one.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in the "},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" the encoder is made with. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals. A record the encoder can’t write is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"starts with "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", as Mixpanel’s own events’ names do, one with a property Mixpanel reads for itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(a "},{"code":"$","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed one, "},{"code":"token","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"time","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"distinct_id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"code":"bucket","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), one of 255 properties or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more counting the encoder’s own, one holding an array of 255 elements or more, one whose property"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nests objects more than 3 deep, one whose event isn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value JSON can’t, one whose timestamp is before 1971 or has no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"epoch-milliseconds form, and one too large for Mixpanel. The destination reports each as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDropReport.skipped(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", a "},{"code":"SkippedRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" whose reason is a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel answers 200 even when it ingests none of a request’s events, and its track API ingests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only events from the last 5 days, so a record older than that when it is sent is counted as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered and not stored. A wrong region, or a token of no project, may be answered 200 with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing stored too, so check the project’s Live View after setting the destination up."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To send to PostHog or Amplitude, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","import MixpanelEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let mixpanel = try HTTPDestination.mixpanel(","    projectToken: projectToken,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu or .india, where the project's data resides","    plan: plan)","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [.sessions()])","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: mixpanel)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers what Mixpanel receives, and why, in more detail."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"]}],"references":{"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/choosingdestinations":{"type":"link","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Choosing Destinations"}],"title":"Choosing Destinations","url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelEncodingError":{"role":"symbol","title":"MixpanelEncodingError","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" couldn’t send a record, which it leaves out of the batch’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requests as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" reports as a drop. When it can encode no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"record of a batch, it makes no request, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" sends nothing for the batch."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelencodingerror","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelEncodingError"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelEncodingError"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelSetupError":{"title":"MixpanelSetupError","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelSetupError","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Why "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"couldn’t make a destination."}],"url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelsetuperror","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MixpanelSetupError"}]},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/MixpanelBatchEncoder/batchLimit":{"title":"batchLimit","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding\/mixpanelbatchencoder\/batchlimit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel’s limits on one request: 2,000 events, 2,000,000 bytes of body, and 999,999 bytes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one event."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/MixpanelBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"batchLimit","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV","text":"BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send records to a Mixpanel project through its track API."}],"role":"collection","title":"MixpanelEncoding","url":"\/documentation\/mixpanelencoding"},"doc://MixpanelEncoding/documentation/MixpanelEncoding/HTTPDestinations/HTTPDestination/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MixpanelEncoding\/documentation\/MixpanelEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:transport:backoff:clock:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":